Z||000000||cscougar||08-08-2001||07:06 PM||||Is there anyone out there who would break down a Fiero steering column and tighten the torx bolts that loosen causing steering column wobble.   My 85 GT is developing this and I have very nice extra column that I could ship to someone to fix since it also has the wobble. <BR> <BR>I know there are instructions out there but I really am afraid of not being able to get it all back together.  I would pay a fair price for the work and for shipping back and forth.<BR> <BR>Thanks<BR> <BR>Ted||||reg||1
Z||000001||starfighter007@msn.com||08-08-2001||07:42 PM||||It really is not that hard or difficult.The hardest part if you can call it hard is having the right tools.Like a wheel puller that you could get from auto zone rent or by the whole set for maybe twenty dollors.Once you pull the steering wheel off it is really simple to get to the area that you need to for tighting those loose screws.If you still dont feel comfortable,I am sure a body shop could do this for you relitively cheap. I think cheaper than shipping It to lets say me here in Phx.Az.But if you decide that you would like to have some body here on the list do it I would do it for the fun of it Provided that you would take care of shipping cost.let me know either way ||||reg||1
